ID=NC000051
BIB_ID=BC000018
TITLE=Origins of Civil Defense
LOCATOR=§3
USE=
TEXT=Twentieth-century civil defense efforts can be traced to the first world war, when Congress authorized the creation of a Council of National Defense to advise the executive branch as to the optimal placement of troops and supplies within the United States in the event of an attack.
